28:  kpharness pioneer reclaim     --out R.toml
29-    Replay committed steps through one attached owner process, which is
30-    then the only engine connection. While it is attached, `step`, `commit`
31:    and `discard` for that route go through it, and `exec`, `reply`,
32:    `state`, `events` and `shots` are refused. `--speed` is the engine's
33-    configured multiplier in (0,16], read back before it is reported; the
34-    prior multiplier is restored at job end unless a route `speed` step ran.
35:    `stop` (or SIGTERM/SIGHUP to the owner) stops execution. It does not
36-    pause the game world. `reclaim` recovers after an owner was killed
37-    without cleanup; it refuses while the owner still holds its locks.
